From: EglantinePS5 <noreply@eglantineps5.local>
Subject: [PATCH] Migrate 0362-lichii-cpu-0232-constant-buffer-word-batches.patch

Source: 0362-lichii-cpu-0232-constant-buffer-word-batches.patch
Core patch. Paths are the submodule's. Applies on core16 alone or in the lichii-cpu order.

Source: zortos293/Lichii PR 184, commit 4a0bc9a007, with bfc3eb523d for the device page limit,
GPL-3.0-or-later. Only the constant buffer part. CallMethodFast is left out: it saves a few
predicted branches per method.

EDEN_NX2_CB_BATCH=1: GpuSplit::Execute looks ahead over up to 64 single writes to const_buffer.buffer
and hands them to Maxwell3D::CallConstBufferWords, one page table walk and one memcpy. Off with
EDEN_NX2_3D_HISTORY, EDEN_NX2_3D_METHODS and EDEN_NX2_GPU_PROFILE. Falls back to one by one over a
device page, at the buffer's end, or inside a macro. Sparse memory stays word by word, and the
accumulator gets the same ranges as before.

Only runs with the split GPU thread (fast GPU on). Helps only if GPUBack is the limit, which nobody
has measured for Ocarina.

Pool memory: none. 512 bytes of stack.

Checked: PS5-target syntax compile of gpu_split and maxwell_3d and memory_manager, no errors. Lichii's
equivalence test needs all of video_core and was not run here. Not run.

